{
  "version": 1,
  "courseId": 1362070,
  "sourceLanguage": "en",
  "targetLanguage": "zh-TW",
  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "25600178",
      "title": "Attaching Payloads to Actions",
      "sourceHash": "c86a51a87bd55f724414ce2d4f77e28c471dd5abb31772667f287d235ab7baf2",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.18,
          "end": 4.95,
          "en": "Let's dig deeper into Redux.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 4.95,
          "end": 8.85,
          "en": "Up to this point, we only dispatched simple actions.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.85,
          "end": 11.55,
          "en": "They only had a type, nothing else.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 11.55,
          "end": 14.78,
          "en": "In reality, you often wanna dispatch actions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 14.78,
          "end": 17.58,
          "en": "that also carry an extra value.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 17.58,
          "end": 19.26,
          "en": "Let's say we wanna add a new button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 19.26,
          "end": 24.26,
          "en": "to the counter component, which says increase by 5.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 24.89,
          "end": 26.95,
          "en": "We could, of course also had a decreased button",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 26.95,
          "end": 29.79,
          "en": "but let's stick to the increase button for now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 29.79,
          "end": 31.92,
          "en": "Now, even though it has this label",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 31.92,
          "end": 34.61,
          "en": "it of course only increases this by one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.61,
          "end": 38.06,
          "en": "because I still just call the incrementHandler here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 38.06,
          "end": 39.593,
          "en": "and dispatch increment.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.6,
          "end": 43.04,
          "en": "Of course, we could now go to the store",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.04,
          "end": 47.63,
          "en": "and prepare our Reducer for another action type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 47.63,
          "end": 49.37,
          "en": "which is increaseby5",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 50.92,
          "end": 55.8,
          "en": "where we then return our updated state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 55.8,
          "end": 58.533,
          "en": "where we increase the state.counter by 5.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 59.46,
          "end": 61.36,
          "en": "But that's not scalable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 61.36,
          "end": 64.08,
          "en": "We can't predict all possible values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 64.08,
          "end": 65.89,
          "en": "we might wanna support.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 65.89,
          "end": 68.55,
          "en": "The counter of course is just a dummy example.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 68.55,
          "end": 71.01,
          "en": "But if you're using this in a real project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 71.01,
          "end": 72.7,
          "en": "which we'll do later in the course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 72.7,
          "end": 76.71000000000001,
          "en": "and you need to work with any user input, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 76.71000000000001,
          "end": 81.003,
          "en": "you can't hard-code those values here in your Reducer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 82.42,
          "end": 85.53,
          "en": "Instead, the action which we dispatch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 85.53,
          "end": 87.37,
          "en": "and which reaches the Reducer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 87.37,
          "end": 90.513,
          "en": "often needs to carry extra data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 91.41,
          "end": 96.41,
          "en": "So that, for example, we have a increase action type here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 96.97,
          "end": 99.42,
          "en": "and that action type",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 99.42,
          "end": 102.44,
          "en": "does not increase the counter by a fixed number,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 102.44,
          "end": 105.61,
          "en": "but instead we expect to get the value",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 105.61,
          "end": 109.28999999999999,
          "en": "by which you wanna increase from the action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 109.28999999999999,
          "end": 111.53,
          "en": "In there we could say that we expect",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 111.53,
          "end": 116.1,
          "en": "to get the value property or have an amount property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 116.1,
          "end": 117.21000000000001,
          "en": "or whatever it is.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 117.21000000000001,
          "end": 119.53,
          "en": "And then we wanna increase by that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 119.53,
          "end": 121.76,
          "en": "That would be a reasonable expectation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 121.76,
          "end": 124.11,
          "en": "And that's of course, a very common scenario",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 124.11,
          "end": 127.163,
          "en": "hence Redux and React Redux supports it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 128.02,
          "end": 131.83,
          "en": "Back in the counter, we can now add a new function here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 131.83,
          "end": 136.82999999999998,
          "en": "the increaseHandler, and in there we again wanna dispatch,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 138.37,
          "end": 141.12,
          "en": "but now the action which we wanna dispatch",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 141.12,
          "end": 143.78,
          "en": "will not just have a type.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 143.78,
          "end": 146.32,
          "en": "It will have one as the type is increase",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 146.32,
          "end": 150.18,
          "en": "but it cannot also get an extra payload,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 150.18,
          "end": 152.7,
          "en": "extra data which it carries.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 152.7,
          "end": 156.28,
          "en": "For example, an extra amount property.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 156.28,
          "end": 159.97,
          "en": "And this property name is entirely up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 159.97,
          "end": 161.74,
          "en": "It's your action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 161.74,
          "end": 163.45,
          "en": "It's your action object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 163.45,
          "end": 166.97,
          "en": "You can add whichever properties you want.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 166.97,
          "end": 169.1,
          "en": "So here I'll add an amount property",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 169.1,
          "end": 171.74,
          "en": "and set amount to 5 here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 171.74,
          "end": 174.37,
          "en": "Of course 5 is therefore still hard-coded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 174.37,
          "end": 177.44,
          "en": "here in this function, but that's just a demo.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 177.44,
          "end": 179.45,
          "en": "Of course, this value could be coming",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 179.45,
          "end": 181.3,
          "en": "from an input field.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 181.3,
          "end": 183.08,
          "en": "Here it's hard-coded",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 183.08,
          "end": 186.763,
          "en": "but now we can point at the increaseHandler here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 189.02,
          "end": 192.15,
          "en": "Now we add this extra payload to the action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 192.15,
          "end": 195.07,
          "en": "and in our store, in the Reducer function,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 195.07,
          "end": 196.81,
          "en": "when the type is increased,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 196.81,
          "end": 200.77,
          "en": "we do expect this amount field on the action.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 200.77,
          "end": 202.787,
          "en": "Therefore, of course, you need to make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 202.787,
          "end": 205.73,
          "en": "that the property you're accessing here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 205.73,
          "end": 207.84,
          "en": "on the action in the Reducer,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 207.84,
          "end": 209.7,
          "en": "has exactly the same name",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 209.7,
          "end": 213.79,
          "en": "as the property you add to the action when you dispatch it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 213.79,
          "end": 216.713,
          "en": "Otherwise you won't be able to extract this data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 218.34,
          "end": 220.84,
          "en": "Hence now, if we save this and reload this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 220.84,
          "end": 225.23,
          "en": "we do increase by five, but now this is very flexible.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 225.23,
          "end": 229.28,
          "en": "We can easily change this to 10 and for completeness sake,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 229.28,
          "end": 232.11,
          "en": "change the button text to 10 as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 232.11,
          "end": 234.39,
          "en": "And now we increase by 10.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 234.39,
          "end": 238.92000000000002,
          "en": "It works just like that because now the Reducer is dynamic.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 238.92000000000002,
          "end": 242.19,
          "en": "It extracts an action payload.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 242.19,
          "end": 245.97,
          "en": "And action payloads are very common, often needed,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 245.97,
          "end": 248.41,
          "en": "and as you see, it's super easy to add them.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 248.41,
          "end": 251.71,
          "en": "It's just an extra property which you add",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 251.71,
          "end": 253.423,
          "en": "to your action objects.",
          "zh": ""
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
  "errors": []
}